findings.body:
**Issue:** Removing `@require_role("admin")` leaves `DELETE /users/<user>` with no authorization. Any client that can hit the route can delete any user.

**Failure mode:** `DELETE /users/alice` (or `bob`, or any name in `USERS`) now reaches `USERS.remove(user)` and returns 204 with no role check. Cleanup jobs that run as `viewer` stop getting 403s because *everyone* is allowed, including anonymous callers.

**Fix:** Keep a server-side authorization check. Grant delete to a dedicated cleanup/service role (or authenticated admin caller), and continue denying `viewer` and unauthenticated requests. Do not leave this route open.

```suggestion
@app.route("/users/<user>", methods=["DELETE"])
@require_role("admin")
def delete_user(user):
```

If cleanup must run as a non-admin identity, extend `require_role` (or add a separate guard) so it authorizes the *caller* from the session/token, and allow only that service account — not the entire viewer role and not the public.
